    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "Born in Niger, Boubé grew up in the village of Iferouane (on the edge of the Ténéré desert), which hosts the most important Tuareg music festival. It is in the hypnotic atmosphere of this village, nestled at the foot of the Tamgak mountains, that Boubé learned music. He sings and plays several instruments characteristic of Tuareg music, a style known internationally as"
      }
